From: SP11 Audio Porting Project <sp11-audio@local>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:18:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6apm: quiesce pull watermarks before soft pause

The first Render-Parity live PAUSE_PUSH reached the DSP, but the expected
PAUSE_COMPLETE event timed out.  PAUSE_COMPLETE and RESUME_COMPLETE were
both delivered only after the ALSA trigger stall ended.

ALSA invokes the trigger callback with the PCM stream lock held.  Leave the
pull stream marked RUNNING while waiting for PAUSE_COMPLETE and an earlier
watermark can call snd_pcm_period_elapsed() on the same serialized GPR
receive path.  That callback waits for the PCM lock held by trigger, so the
later completion event cannot be dispatched to release trigger.

Enter the stopped host state before sending the pause parameter.  The pull
watermark handler then skips snd_pcm_period_elapsed(), allowing the exact
DSP PAUSE_COMPLETE event to reach the waiter.  Restore RUNNING if the pause
command itself is rejected.  Resume already remains stopped until its
completion event succeeds.

This ordering also matches the recovered Windows lifecycle: PAUSE/state 3
precedes the value-1 SOFT_PAUSE TKV.

Signed-off-by: SP11 Audio Porting Project <sp11-audio@local>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -391,10 +391,23 @@ static int q6apm_dai_sp11_soft_pause(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	if (!prtd->graph->pull_mode)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
+	/*
+	 * ALSA calls trigger() with the PCM stream lock held.  A pull watermark
+	 * delivered while that lock is held must not call snd_pcm_period_elapsed()
+	 * ahead of the SOFT_PAUSE completion event on the same GPR receive path,
+	 * or completion delivery is blocked behind the trigger waiter.  Windows
+	 * likewise enters PAUSE/state 3 before it sends the value-1 TKV.
+	 */
+	if (pause)
+		prtd->state = Q6APM_STREAM_STOPPED;
+
 	reinit_completion(done);
 	ret = q6apm_graph_sp11_soft_pause(prtd->graph, pause);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		if (pause)
+			prtd->state = Q6APM_STREAM_RUNNING;
 		return ret;
+	}
 
 	/* The DSP accepted the command. Track requested state even if its
 	 * completion event is delayed/lost so STOP can safely clean up a
-- 
2.51.0
